    dcterms:identifier "P157005" ;
    rdfs:comment "The maximum context window refers to the maximum number of tokens that a language model can consider at once when processing input data. It defines the length of the input sequence that the model can handle in a single forward pass. In the context of SLMs, the maximum context window varies across different models, ranging from 1k to 128k."@en ;
